# /mnt/bench/work -- benchmark tooling repo.
#
# FAIL-SAFE POLICY: ignore EVERYTHING, then explicitly allow only the tooling
# files. New files (data dirs, credentials, downloaded assets) are ignored by
# default, so nothing sensitive can be tracked by accident. To track a new
# tooling file, add an explicit `!` allow-rule below AND confirm it holds no
# secrets or trial data.

/*

# --- explicitly tracked tooling (safe to push) ---
!.gitignore
!CLAUDE.md
!README.md
!run-bench.sh
!analyze_tokens.py
!agents
!fixtures

# --- junk inside allowed dirs ---
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.bak

# NEVER TRACKED (already covered by `/*`, listed for intent + defense in depth):
#   secrets.env            -- live Claude Code OAuth token
#   *.credentials.json      -- Claude Code credentials
#   auth.json               -- iris auth store
#   jobs/                   -- trial data (may embed uploaded creds / token
#                              fragments in logs + agent transcripts; also huge)
#   assets/                 -- large iris binaries / tarballs (regenerable)
secrets.env
*.credentials.json
auth.json
jobs/
assets/
